7. Explain the concept of Double Pointer.
Ans:
 A double pointer is a pointer that stores the address of another pointer. It is also called a pointer to a pointer.
It is declared using two asterisks:
int **p;
Here, p is a double pointer. It stores the address of a pointer variable.
Double pointers are useful when a pointer itself needs to be accessed or modified through another pointer.

